--
Was KNOWNBUG with the headers of libstdc++ 16 (gcc 16) only (silent wrong
result: assertions 2 and 3 FAILURE without any front-end diagnostic).  Fixed by
round 160/161: `__builtin_clzg', `<=>' on pointers (strong_ordering), and the
static-member-template-of-a-base / braced-init / constexpr-array fixes that
made <compare>'s comparison-category helpers type-check.  Runs where the host
gcc is >= 16 (tag libstdcxx16).
Round 162: no system-header body is dropped any more (rewritten comparison
candidates from <=>, the constrained conversion function template of
__max_size_type, and its constructor template's specializations no longer
competing as converting constructors).
